DusdPegOracleCurve::rawPoolState()
├── given an underlying pool read reverts
│   ├── when ma_last_time reverts
│   │   └── it should bubble the pool revert
│   ├── when get_balances reverts
│   │   └── it should bubble the pool revert
│   ├── when get_p(0) reverts
│   │   └── it should bubble the pool revert
│   ├── when last_price(0) reverts
│   │   └── it should bubble the pool revert
│   ├── when ema_price(0) reverts
│   │   └── it should bubble the pool revert
│   ├── when price_oracle(0) reverts
│   │   └── it should bubble the pool revert
│   ├── when ma_exp_time reverts
│   │   └── it should bubble the pool revert
│   ├── when A_precise reverts
│   │   └── it should bubble the pool revert
│   └── when future_A reverts
│       └── it should bubble the pool revert
├── given every underlying pool read succeeds
│   ├── when get_balances returns an empty array
│   │   └── it should revert with array-out-of-bounds panic 0x32
│   ├── when get_balances returns an array with one element
│   │   └── it should revert with array-out-of-bounds panic 0x32
│   ├── when get_balances returns exactly two elements
│   │   ├── it should set quoteTokenBalance from element 0
│   │   └── it should set dusdBalance from element 1
│   ├── when get_balances returns more than two elements
│   │   ├── it should set balances from elements 0 and 1
│   │   └── it should ignore every additional element
│   ├── it should call get_p with ORACLE_INDEX and return it as currentStatePriceWad
│   ├── it should call last_price with ORACLE_INDEX and return it as lastStatePriceWad
│   ├── it should call ema_price with ORACLE_INDEX and return it as storedEmaPriceWad
│   ├── it should call price_oracle with ORACLE_INDEX and return it as currentEmaPriceWad
│   ├── it should decode the low 128 timestamp bits as priceUpdatedAt
│   ├── it should decode the high 128 timestamp bits as invariantUpdatedAt
│   ├── it should return ma_exp_time as maExpTime
│   ├── it should return A_precise as aPrecise
│   ├── it should return future_A as futureAPrecise
│   └── when prices, timestamps or controller configuration values are zero or inconsistent
│       └── it should return the raw values without validation
└── given any successful execution
    ├── it should not modify contract state
    └── it should not emit events
